{
  "_schema_version": 1,
  "env_id": "PullCubeTool-v1",
  "roles": {
    "movable": "actor:l_shape_tool",
    "destination": "actor:cube",
    "reference": "actor:table-workspace"
  },
  "notes": [
    "No goal entity exists; success is the cube's coordinate passing a threshold. planar-distance(cube, table-workspace) is a proxy: the table origin sits at XY ~(-0.12, 0), essentially the robot base, so the cube closing on it is the pull making progress. Dense signal only, never a success detector.",
    "Measured over 5 successful demonstrations, the proxy moves monotonically inward every time but its absolute level does not track success: episodes start at 0.252-0.332 m (4/5 'far', 1/5 already 'medium') and succeed anywhere from 0.245 m ('medium') to 0.065 m ('very-near'). So the pull phase carries only 0.15 -- at the 0.45 it was first given, two equally successful episodes would have differed by 0.30 in terminal Phi*, teaching the head that some successes are worth a third of others. The weight moved to reach_cube, where contact at 99.9% presence makes the endpoint unambiguous.",
    "The 'medium' rung is deliberately the smallest: one episode in five starts there, so it is partly a starting condition rather than an achievement.",
    "support-compatibility(cube, l_shape_tool) is absent: the support bucket was excluded at 15.7% presence, so no components back it and it would score unobserved forever.",
    "height-offset is not used for the pull: the cube slides along the table, so its height never changes."
  ],
